 "notes": "New 95% CL limit on c_gamma/Lambda (c_gamma=1, c_g=0) set by this paper's bump hunt of the published PrimEx carbon-target m_gammagamma spectrum (Fig. 2 of arXiv:1009.1681), shown as the dark-blue shaded regions in Fig. 2 (prim_lims.pdf); extracted from the vector fill path of the e-print figure. g_agamma = c_gamma/Lambda exactly, since the paper uses Gamma(a->gg) = c_gamma^2 m_a^3/(64 pi Lambda^2), matching L = -(g/4) a F Fdual. The excluded region consists of two islands, 0.110-0.125 GeV and 0.145-0.160 GeV, separated by the pi0 mass veto; vertical edges are represented by points at the plot-top value 1e-2 GeV^-1. The PrimEx and GlueX projection curves and the separate ALP-gluon (GlueX) limit are not reported. Not a dark-matter search, so no density rescaling.",
